                    <note type="editorial">
  It is difficult to be wholly certain about the identification - the  <title>DNB</title> does confirm that Pierre Condé was in
  London at the time (all 19 contacts 1802-5) and the context is often artistic (eg. calls in conjunction with
    <persName key="NOR01"> Northcote</persName>). However, this is also a period in which Godwin meets the <persName key="CAR09">Abbé Carron</persName>
    who has links to Prince and Princess Condé, relatives of Louis Philippe II d'Orléans, known during the revolution as Philippe Egalité.  The circumstantial evidence, however, points to the artist.

  </note>
